+CytoSPACE provides two mechanisms for plotting output heatmaps. The first are heatmaps generated by default when running CytoSPACE. By default, the geometry and plotting parameters have been optimized for standard 10x Visium spatial slides. To plot non-Visium spatial data, the "plot-Visium" flag should be set to False. As an example, to change the plotting parameters, e.g., -nr (number of rows), -nc (number of coulmns), -ss (spot size), -pm (plot marker whcih indicates the shape of the spots) and -pv (plot Visium), from command line, for the melanoma dataset:
